  "deletedAt": null,
  "deletedBy": null,
  "details": "Since we know that native face tracking can be done on Desktop, and native eye tracking is done on VR, is it possible to be able to override visemes blend shapes with the VRCFT blend shapes used for the models with built in face tracking? \n\nFace tracking alone can take up to 165 parameter space in a mode, crippling users' ability to create more onto a model, and sometimes forced to create numerous versions of the same model. This idea would eliminate the issue that a lot of us users face when creating a model with face tracking\n\nIt can probably be done if the code looks for VRCFT blend shapes *first* then if it's not there, it pulls from the visemes instead. \n\nIf possible, can this be put in-game? Seeing how hand tracking can also be native, I am sure it's easy to grab the face tracking blend shapes from a model as it is already there.",
